{:edb/db-before-t 2711 :edb/db-after-t 2712 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536024 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:06:23.087Z" 13194139536024 true] [17592186166822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379818 13194139536024 true] [17592186166823 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379832 13194139536024 true] [17592186166824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379825 13194139536024 true] [17592186167036 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536024 true] [17592186167036 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x) = 2x_{1}^{2} - 3x_{2}^{2} - x_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖ = 1$." 13194139536024 false] [17592186167036 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186167036 1145 "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-3(1)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-3.$ But before we conclude that $-3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-3.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-3(1)^{2}-(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-3.$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186167038 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536024 true] [17592186167038 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x) = 7x_{1}^{2} + 8x_{2}^{2} + 5x_{3}^{2} - 4x_{2}x_{3}$ given that $‖x‖ = 1$." 13194139536024 false] [17592186167038 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=7{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186167038 1145 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,7,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=4.\n$$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379818 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379819 13194139536024 true] [17592186379818 1089 "q-138021" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379818 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536024 true] [17592186379818 1100 "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379818 1113 #uuid "e597502b-9616-570d-85d2-53bc922c89a6" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379818 1145 "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-4{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379820 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379821 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379822 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379823 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379824 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1041 "selection" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379820 13194139536024 true] [17592186379819 1110 #uuid "5a1a0e64-0272-581c-b947-b7159d4ba4d3" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379820 1034 "2" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379820 1111 #uuid "783b1f87-c0c1-52ab-b346-f4b0e7ffa15c" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379821 1034 "6" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379821 1111 #uuid "af575672-518e-5c18-97a4-7800770c87bd" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379822 1034 "-4" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379822 1111 #uuid "cf9bbfe3-7cda-58d8-9e59-d2b23e980625" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379823 1034 "4" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379823 1111 #uuid "570fa96e-3f08-52ec-a22c-f6cbf778bccb" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379824 1034 "-2" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379824 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379824 1111 #uuid "403c9b07-0dbf-5f77-9560-97c8f7accf6d" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379825 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379826 13194139536024 true] [17592186379825 1089 "q-138075" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379825 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536024 true] [17592186379825 1100 "Find the  maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379825 1113 #uuid "f07b8c52-650b-58ad-8dad-c02bf167a0ab" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379825 1145 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,2,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=3.\n$$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379827 13194139536024 true] [17592186379826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379828 13194139536024 true] [17592186379826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379829 13194139536024 true] [17592186379826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379830 13194139536024 true] [17