{2} \\\\  & \\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=3.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}+6(0)^{2}+4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $3.$" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379834 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379835 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379836 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379837 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379838 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1041 "selection" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379834 13194139536024 true] [17592186379833 1110 #uuid "b937ceeb-0702-54ca-b035-2404b89bb3d5" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379834 1034 "3" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379834 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379834 1111 #uuid "63be96b9-041a-53cd-aecf-b20ee1f44375" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379835 1034 "6" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379835 1111 #uuid "b50f7c23-2861-5c61-9b1a-75dc826db19f" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379836 1034 "1" 13194139536024 true] [17592186379836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536024 true] [17592186379836 1111 #uuid "a4a8027a-b384-551a-9e90-c6f1eb741c9d" 13194139536024 true] [